<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Intrinsic dimension estimates (mean <math id="A8.T6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> std) for different methods and values of <math id="A8.T6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from Fig <a href="#A7.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ G.8 Effect of hyper-parameters ‣ Appendix G Additional experiments and plots ‣ Quantum-inspired Benchmark for Estimating Intrinsic Dimension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> that the true ID of the butterfly is <math id="A8.T6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=1.445" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.445</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=1.445</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A8.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01335v1/plots/hofs_ide.png" id="A8.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:426/494;" width="426" height="494" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 19: </span>Red dashed line indicates the actual fractal dimension. Row indicates same <math id="A8.F19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, column refers to same method. Note how ABID produces reliable ID estimates for small <math id="A8.F19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, while most other methods return LID estimates very different from the fractal dimension. <math id="A8.F19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1000</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
